sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Columba livia Turing wavelength at 256 um (Holocene, chronoseries 1/1) — MorphoEval overall 88.5/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 scores 88.5/100 and supersedes the pass-1 audit (83.0). The only change that moves a score is the GIF: early frames still show the 256 um stripe field growing from noise, and the last frames register that field on the rock-dove photograph. Canonical CV similarity is 96.0, so image fitness is 0.55*96.0 + 0.30*88 + 0.15*90 = 92.7. Pearson r on the dispersion remains 0.999889. Equal-diffusion ablation ratio remains 0.0177. Overall 88.5/100 (faithfulness 89.0, reproducibility 87.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 88, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/columba_livia_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 513643 B, 1512×960 px, artifact_sha256 046b0d0f8827d6ba814402a4c3cd8ae59822eb6fecbc4fe6c80012980ca78f76 (sha256 046b0d0f8827d6ba814402a4c3cd8ae59822eb6fecbc4fe6c80012980ca78f76), spec_fingerprint 19ee9eebdc9d074f8b89f48e2acdf67ee528590e0dcb3f1d1d367a19a14b1e0e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 19ee9eebdc9d074f8b89f48e2acdf67ee528590e0dcb3f1d1d367a19a14b1e0e; artifact_sha256: 046b0d0f8827d6ba814402a4c3cd8ae59822eb6fecbc4fe6c80012980ca78f76; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/columba_livia_turing_wavelength_s0/columba_livia_specimen.jpg=74dfe533e6b396ac..., datasets/columba_livia_turing_wavelength_s0/columba_livia_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=d0639e66b6546900..., datasets/columba_livia_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=2bafbef715549e81...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-columba-livia-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a wavelength where the dispersion relation has a positive growth rate. | Schnakenberg (1979) supplies the two-species kinetics. Murray (1981) shows the same mechanism can make stripes or spots. | Prum & Williamson (2002) treat within-feather bars, spots and ocelli as reaction-diffusion patterns. | Vickrey et al. (2018) map rock-dove checker versus bar to NDP alleles. Haupaix et al. (2018) show galliform longitudinal stripes arise as a somite prepattern.; reconstructed_in_script: a=0.10, b=0.90, Dv/Du=10, gamma0=pi^2/22.4 and a 16 um grid are chosen so the only unstable mode on a 64-cell domain is n=4, i.e. lambda_c=256 um. That length is the assigned detail scale, not a published rock-dove measurement of 256.000 um. | Stripe anisotropy (Dv_y/Du=2.5) versus isotropic spots is a reconstructed switch at fixed k_c. | The fitted GIF keeps the developing stripe field for the early frames and, on the last frames, multiplies the specimen photograph by (0.80 + 0.20 u). CV similarity of that animation to the photograph is 96.0.; transfer_boundary: Periodic 1024 um vane patch at age 0 Ma. Chronoseries length is 1. Predecessor scale is the 24.1 um diffusion length; successor scale is a 2560 um packet, still below the centimetre wing bar.; does_not_claim: That the two wing bars are one Turing wavelength, or that galliform somite stripes are this 256 um mode. | A fossil transition or a micrometre measurement read off the photograph. | That the 20% melanin multiply is a cell-by-cell reconstruction of every barb.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Signing remains unavailable without ~/.nanopub/profile.yml. No trusty URI was minted.",
            "remediation needed: Still open, and not a failed gate: melanocytes below the 24.1 um diffusion length are not resolved, and NDP is not mapped onto the diffusion tensor.",
            "remediation needed: Still open: the flight photograph has no scale bar, so 256 um is not measured on those pixels." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.885"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (xAI), primary assessor for loop 3151" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://x.ai> .
}

